; THE CLAN HOLD (the 2026-08-28 layout rebuild) - Frostfang Reach's only settlement.
;
; WARNING WHAT THIS REPLACED. Two longhouses mirrored at x = +/-12, a moot hall centred on the axis
; behind them, three tents, four braziers in two mirrored pairs, and the three crafting stations in a
; huddle at (-8, 1). Everything the hold had stood inside one rectangle and the road ran through it.
;
; THE LAYOUT NOW - a ring, not a row, and the roads go ROUND it rather than through it:
;   THE MOOT RING    an oval of open ground centred (-4, 2), about 22 x 18. The moot fire is at its
;                    heart and the chief stands beside it. Three buildings close it in a broken arc:
;                    the moot hall at (2, -12) on the north, the two longhouses angled at 55 and 115
;                    degrees on the west. Nothing in the ring is parallel to anything else.
;   THE WORK TERRACE x 8..24, z -8..8, off the EAST road: forge, workbench, alchemy bench, the
;                    quartermaster and the hearthkeeper. The road runs along its south edge, so a
;                    trader reaches trade without entering the ring at all.
;   THE BEAST RUNS   x -28..-18, z -6..10, along the WEST road: three tents, a brazier and the beast
;                    tamer. The same idea on the other side and deliberately a different shape - a
;                    strip rather than a court.
;   THE NORTH GATE   the glacier road comes in at (0, -30) and has to bend EAST round the back of the
;                    moot hall before it reaches the ring, so the hold is never visible from the pass.
;   THE EXILE        (18, 22), his fire at (20, 24) - outside everything, in the south-east, with no
;                    road to him. He is not part of the hold and the layout now says so.
;   rock and pine    four rock clusters and the pines wall the south and the north-east. WARNING FOUR
;                    prp_glacier masses used to stand here too, two of them beside the west road at
;                    the hold's own entrance, and they were the first thing a player saw on arriving:
;                    five-metre pale blue slabs of one repeated model, reading as crates. The terrain
;                    walls the hold now - that is what the ridges either side of it are for - so the
;                    ice went. Ice belongs in the pass, where it is the subject rather than the wall.
;
; WARNING THREE SEAMS, AND THEY ARE ARITHMETIC. West (-30, 0) meets the wild dragon roost, east
; (30, 0) the ash roost, north (0, -30) the glacier pass. The region spawn at world (100, 1.2, 0) is
; cell-local (0, 20). The block above Presentation_clan_hold in data/regions/FrostfangReach.tres
; carries the arithmetic for all three.
;
; WARNING FOUR SCHEDULES WERE MIGRATED WITH THIS REBUILD (ClanChief, ClanQuartermaster,
; ClanBeastTamer, ClanHearthkeeper). They author RAW WORLD destinations - Origin is zero on all four,
; unlike the Embermarket's - and this cell sits at world (100, 0, -20), so a point read out of this
; file is world = local + (100, 0, -20). Getting that backwards is the 37C placement bug in miniature.
;
; WARNING EVERYTHING STATIC PARENTS TO Nav; the NPCs, the waystone, the stations and the exile's fire
; do not. A body inside the NavigationRegion3D is a hole in the navmesh where a person is standing.

; ⚠️ THE NAV VOXEL GRID COARSENED WITH THE WORLD (the 2026-08-29 geography overhaul). Cells
; went from 52 m squares on a flat slab to 90-200 m of real terrain, and a 0.25 m voxel over
; five times the area is twenty-five times the columns to rasterise — the traversal probe timed
; out waiting for the bake. ⚠️ AND THE agent_* DIMS DID NOT FOLLOW. On the 0.25 grid 1.75 and
; 0.5 were whole voxels; on this one they are not, so every bake quantised them and warned. The
; values below are the QUANTISED ones, so the file now says what the bake does: agent_height and
; agent_radius CEIL to a voxel (cell_height / cell_size), agent_max_climb FLOORS to cell_height.
; ⚠️ They encode this grid — change cell_size or cell_height and recompute all three with it.
[sub_resource type="NavigationMesh" id="NavMesh_hold"]
geometry_parsed_geometry_type = 1
cell_size = 0.3
cell_height = 0.3
agent_height = 1.8
agent_radius = 0.6
agent_max_climb = 0.3
agent_max_slope = 42.0

